verses.text:
Judith said:
Lead off for my God with tambourines,
sing to the Lord with cymbals;
weave for him a psalm and a song of praise;
exalt him, and call upon his name.

For the Lord is a God who crushes wars;{a}
he set his camp in the midst of his people
and snatched me from the hand of my pursuers.

Then my lowly ones shouted for joy,
and my weak ones cried aloud, and the enemy cowered;{d}
they lifted their voices, and the enemy was routed.

Sons of slave girls pierced them through;
they wounded them like the children of deserters.
They perished before the battle line of my Lord.

For every sacrifice as a fragrant aroma is a small thing,
and all the fat for burnt offerings to you a very little thing;
but the one who reveres the Lord stands great for all time.
